  "item": "fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]/impl[GraphWithChangingEdges/Contents]/fn[fingerprint]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "Contents is required by validation, but this regression\n observes only the outgoing-edge selection. No node contents\n are read, so producing a content fingerprint would violate the\n asserted selection-only dependencies."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]/impl[GraphWithChangingEdges/Contents]/fn[fingerprint]` is a valid coverage exception.\n\n- **Placement:** The citation is on an explicitly declared function with a body. Its commentary is in a fenced citation, so it counts as a tracked justification.\n- **Substance:** The commentary gives a real reason, not just difficulty. `Contents` requires `fingerprint`, but this test is meant to observe only outgoing-edge selections. A call to it would mean an unwanted content read, and the `panic!` body acts as a guard against that.\n- **Agreement with the source:**\n  - In `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs`, `Contents::fingerprint` is called only from `InspectionContext::prepare_read`, which reads node content, and from `dependencies_are_current`, for `Dependency::Node`.\n  - The test's agent only calls `outgoing_edges`. The recorded dependency is `Dependency::OutgoingEdges`, checked against `edge_fingerprint`. `edge_fingerprint` hashes target paths through `Graph::node_path` and does not use `Contents::fingerprint`.\n  - The test `node_content` and `format_node_content` bodies also panic, so the test asserts selection-only dependencies. The commentary's claim that no content fingerprint is produced agrees with this.",
